{
  "_README": [
    "The model import's tools, which the app downloads on the user's request (Settings > AI > Model",
    "import tools, or the Download button on Randall's import card) instead of the installer carrying them:",
    "Blender 4 for rigswap's Collada -> GLB step, a CPython 3.13 for rigswap itself, and the wheels it needs",
    "(bpy, numpy, pillow...). docs/dev/MODEL_IMPORT_TOOLS.md is the design.",
    "",
    "Everything comes from the official sources, each file pinned by URL, sha256 and size and checked before it",
    "is unpacked (backend/randall/model_import/tools/assemble.py): download.blender.org, python.org (Windows) or",
    "python-build-standalone (macOS, Linux), and files.pythonhosted.org. Nothing is hosted by us.",
    "",
    "`platforms` is GENERATED: edit `pin` (or pass versions) and run",
    "    python tools/build/pin_model_import_tools.py",
    "which reads every URL, sha256 and size from the publishers. Nobody types a hash. The wheel versions are",
    "utility/rigswap.requirements.txt's, the one list. The layout of each platform's downloads (archive root,",
    "entrypoint, trim list, the paths that must survive the unpack) is LAYOUT in that script.",
    "",
    "Installed under the user's data folder, tools/model-import/: blender/<version>/ and runtime/<key>/ (key: a",
    "hash of the python entry and the wheels list, so an app update that changes neither downloads nothing), and",
    "receipt.json.",
    "",
    "`on_disk` (per platform) is what a real install measured on disk per piece, the Settings card's size before the",
    "download: Blender by its sha256, the runtime by its key, each from an install's receipt.json, recorded with",
    "    python tools/build/pin_model_import_tools.py --measured <receipt.json>...",
    "A re-pin keeps a piece's size while its downloads stay the same and drops it when they move; the app then",
    "estimates that piece from per-format ratios (assemble.ON_DISK) until a new install is measured.",
    "",
    "BLENDER VERSION PIN: 4.3 is what rigswap is developed and measured with: its Collada->GLB conversion runs",
    "here (RIGSWAP_BLENDER4). 4.2.23 crashed natively inside its Collada import on 4 of 24 conversions of the",
    "vanilla Samus, Ganondorf and Kirby exports, 4.3.2 on none (2026-10-29). Do not move it without a real import",
    "on every platform and preparing every fighter target from scratch with it (rigswap's melee.prepare).",
    "PYTHON: 3.13 and bpy 5.2.2 are what rigswap's pyproject requires.",
    "",
    "BLENDER TRIM (Windows and Linux): whole files and folders deleted after the unpack: debug symbols, UI",
    "translations, the Cycles addon's Python/kernel tree and Blender's own python executable. rigswap only",
    "converts DAE to GLB in it; nothing raytraces. Measured on Windows: 971 MB unpacked -> 729 MB. MEASURED AND",
    "REVERTED, do not re-add: oslexec.dll, oslcomp.dll, the OpenImageDenoise_* DLLs, cycles_kernel_oneapi_aot.dll",
    "and anything in blender.shared/ sit in blender.exe's import table (official builds compile Cycles into the",
    "executable; the addon folder is only its UI), and deleting any one stops Blender from starting. Everything",
    "the pipeline touches stays: numpy and the rest of python/lib, io_scene_gltf2, colormanagement (Blender will",
    "not start without config.ocio), fonts, studiolights. macOS keeps Blender.app whole: deleting files inside a",
    "signed bundle breaks its seal."
  ],
